A||N||4||chris6878||will a 2.5 fiero 4cy fit in a 88 Berreta?||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||03-26-2000||12:19 AM||||I was just offered a 88 Berreta for $400 with a bad valve... it has the 2.0 4cly engine.. i can get it cheaper though...     but i was wondering if a 2.5 DIS engine from an 87 fiero would fit in place of the 2.0 DIS in the berreta?  I know that it will bolt to the tranny the same but..  what about the location of the oil filter and stuff.. will this work?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||03-26-2000||01:06 PM||||The aluminum 2.0 is not directly compatible with the cast 2.5. The 2.5 is signifigantly taller for a sart. The 2.5 uses a 700 TBI injector, the 2.0 is multiport as I recall.<P>As long as the valve is not broken off which would trash the whole cylinder, then it would be easier to replace the head.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||03-27-2000||02:26 AM||||There are a TON of 2.0 Berettas & Cavaliers in the junkyards (at least here in Colorado), so I would just buy a good used motor and throw it in.  You should be able to get one for around $200 from a U-Pull-It type of yard.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||03-27-2000||02:32 AM||||thanks  for the replies..  my sis is the one actually looking for a car..  why would i need one? i have 3 fieros...  hahaha  but the car seems to be well worth $400..  hard to get a good running car nowadays for less than $1000 anyway..  <P>thanks again..<BR>chris||||reg||6
Z||000004||TalShino||03-27-2000||08:42 AM||||I got a good running 87 Fiero coupe for 350.00$.. with a none running 84 thrown in the deal.. of course the 87 had been wrecked and didn't have a title.. but hehe.. I found a good looking 88coupe (with title <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) for 200.00$ .... so basicly had me a 88 for 550$ not bad||||reg||1
